**Describe the bug**
Dear all, during the development of an SDK for C# I found a communication problem between the Numaflow part and the ASP WebApplication framework.
The ASP framework blocks all Numaflow http calls with this error
```
HTTP/2 stream error "PROTOCOL_ERROR". A Reset is being sent to the stream.
      Microsoft.AspNetCore.Connections.ConnectionAbortedException: Invalid Host header: '[::]:50051'
```

The Host header is invalid because '[::]:50051' is like '0.0.0.0:50051'. Here the Numaflow code grpc.rs:

```
pub(crate) async fn connect_with_uds(uds_path: PathBuf) -> error::Result<Channel> {
    let channel = Endpoint::try_from("http://[::]:50051")
        .map_err(|e| Error::Connection(format!("Failed to create endpoint: {e:?}")))?
        .connect_with_connector(service_fn(move |_: Uri| {
            let uds_socket = uds_path.clone();
            async move {
                Ok::<_, std::io::Error>(hyper_util::rt::TokioIo::new(
                    UnixStream::connect(uds_socket).await?,
                ))
            }
        }))
        .await
        .map_err(|e| Error::Connection(format!("Failed to connect: {e}")))?;
    Ok(channel)
}

```
The control is executed during the http request parsing so no lucky to insert all control bypass in the code.

The method try_from set the Host header to http://[::]:50051

I suggest to change the value with http://[::1]:50051 or to permit a custom value using configuration or a metadata in the ServerInfo file.



