## Describe the bug
In the current implementation of `VisitParameter`, the parameter is named `p`, which does not match the base class declaration. This can lead to confusion and reduces code readability.

## Afected file:
`FlowSynx.Application/Extensions/PredicateBuilder.cs` lines: 81-87

## Current Code
```csharp
protected override Expression VisitParameter(ParameterExpression p)
{
    if (_map.TryGetValue(p, out var replacement))
        p = replacement;

    return base.VisitParameter(p);
}
```

## Proposed Change
Rename the parameter `p` to `node` to align with the base class and improve clarity:

```csharp
protected override Expression VisitParameter(ParameterExpression node)
{
    if (_map.TryGetValue(node, out var replacement))
        node = replacement;

    return base.VisitParameter(node);
}
```

## Benefits
- Improves code readability  
- Matches the base class declaration for consistency  
- Reduces potential confusion for new contributors

